cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these ontologies, please cite them as below."
type: dataset
title: "Membership and Fraternal Ontologies"
abstract: >-
  Two layered OWL 2 DL and SKOS ontologies for describing membership
  organisations as Linked Open Data. The Membership Organisations Ontology
  (https://w3id.org/membership) covers any membership organisation, closed or
  open: clubs, societies, student nations, associations, political parties and
  trade unions. It models memberships and their lifecycle, admission and fees,
  offices and terms of office, gatherings, distinctions and premises. The
  Fraternal Orders and Sororities Ontology (https://w3id.org/fraternal) extends
  it with degree systems, lodges and grand bodies, ceremonies, insignia, and
  recognition between orders.
authors:
  - family-names: Almgren
    given-names: Oscar
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-6239-5346"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-01
